# Testing

- Test the real risk of the change. Avoid vacuous assertions and duplicate coverage of the same risk.
- Prefer state-transition, boundary, contract, and concurrency cases when those risks exist.
- Mocks do not prove PostgreSQL or Kafka properties — use Testcontainers / broker proof when those boundaries matter.
- Match proof intensity to lane (skill `debina-runtime-proof-testing`): FAST = targeted + `verify-fast`; STANDARD = targeted + integration/contract + review; DECISION/CRITICAL = full runtime proof chain when justified.
- Playwright follows ADR-N16 sequencing; it is not automatic for every task.
- Never claim a test passed unless the exact command ran successfully.
